q .721569 .776471 .819608 RG .4 w 46.8 38.16 m 565.2 38.16 l S .356863 .396078 .45098 rg BT 8.64 TL/F1 7.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 46.8 25.2 Tm (BEYONDX )Tj[-4779.9997]TJ ( | Oracle 19c on Exadata to Amazon Aurora MySQL 8.0)Tj T* ET BT 1 0 0 1 542.3832 25.2 Tm (Page 2)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 722.36 cm .090196 .211765 .364706 rg BT 19 TL/F2 16 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 3 Tm (Executive Summary)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 648.36 cm .14902 .196078 .219608 rg BT 13 TL/F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 55.9 Tm (Modernizing approximately 50 TB of Oracle 19c data from an Oracle Exadata environment to Amazon Aurora MySQL 8.0 was)Tj T* (not a database-copy exercise. The source platform had evolved since the 1990s and embodied more than three and a half)Tj T* (decades of application development, database engineering, operational refinement, and institutional knowledge. The central)Tj T* (challenge was therefore not merely to move data, but to ensure that required business functionality and operational capability)Tj T* (survived a change of database engine and performance architecture.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 576.36 cm .14902 .196078 .219608 rg BT 13 TL/F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 55.9 Tm (AWS Schema Conversion Tool \(AWS SCT\) accelerated assessment and generated an initial target-model skeleton, but)Tj T* -.030554 Tw (production readiness required extensive manual engineering. The team reviewed tables, keys, partitioning, functional indexes,)Tj T* 0 Tw (constraints, triggers, procedures, jobs, archival logic, nested structures, application dependencies, performance behavior, and)Tj T* (fallback requirements. AWS Database Migration Service \(AWS DMS\) provided Full Load + CDC for forward migration and)Tj T* (reverse CDC during the controlled fallback window.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 57.6 530.96 cm .917647 .94902 .972549 rg 0 38.4 82.8 -38.4 re f* .972549 .984314 .992157 rg 82.8 38.4 414 -38.4 re f* q 1 0 0 1 8 14.7 cm .090196 .211765 .364706 rg BT 9 TL/F2 7.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 3.6025 1.5 Tm (CORE POSITION)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 90.8 8 cm .14902 .196078 .219608 rg BT 11.2 TL/F2 8.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 5.3108 13.8 Tm (At ~50 TB scale, migration success depends on preserving business capability, re-engineering)Tj T* 30.0097 0 Td (target behavior, and proving the result with production-representative evidence.)Tj T* ET Q q .721569 .776471 .819608 RG 1 J 1 j .8 w 0 38.4 m 496.8 38.4 l S 0 0 m 496.8 0 l S 0 0 m 0 38.4 l S 496.8 0 m 496.8 38.4 l S .4 w 82.8 0 m 82.8 38.4 l S Q Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 503.96 cm .184314 .458824 .709804 rg BT 14 TL/F2 11.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 2.5 Tm T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 471.96 cm .14902 .196078 .219608 rg BT 13 TL/F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 7 16.9 Tm <7f20>Tj/F2 9.1 Tf (35+ years of capability preservation:)Tj/F1 9.1 Tf ( manual analysis was explicitly used to ensure that functionality embedded since)Tj T* 7 0 Td (the 1990s was not lost.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 439.96 cm .14902 .196078 .219608 rg BT 13 TL/F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 7 16.9 Tm <7f20>Tj/F2 9.1 Tf (Oracle Exadata to Aurora performance transition:)Tj/F1 9.1 Tf ( tuning moved from an Oracle/Exadata ecosystem to workload-driven)Tj T* 7 0 Td (Aurora MySQL engineering.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 407.96 cm .14902 .196078 .219608 rg BT 13 TL/F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 7 16.9 Tm <7f20>Tj/F2 9.1 Tf (Production-simulated performance testing:)Tj/F1 9.1 Tf ( high-CPU SQL and long-running transactions were captured, analyzed, and)Tj T* 7 0 Td (used to design composite indexes.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 375.96 cm .14902 .196078 .219608 rg BT 13 TL/F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 7 16.9 Tm <7f20>Tj/F2 9.1 Tf (Aurora capacity and parameter engineering:)Tj/F1 9.1 Tf ( the target used )Tj/F4 9.1 Tf (db.r8g.24xlarge)Tj/F1 9.1 Tf ( with deliberate parameter tuning for)Tj T* 7 0 Td (concurrency, observability, temporary-table capacity, and CDC.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 343.96 cm .14902 .196078 .219608 rg BT 13 TL/F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 7 16.9 Tm <7f20>Tj/F2 9.1 Tf (Reverse CDC prerequisites:)Tj/F1 9.1 Tf ( Aurora binary logging and retention were engineered so Aurora could act as the source)Tj T* 7 0 Td (during fallback.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 311.96 cm .14902 .196078 .219608 rg BT 13 TL/F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 7 16.9 Tm <7f20>Tj/F2 9.1 Tf (Index lifecycle governance:)Tj/F1 9.1 Tf ( redundant and potentially unused indexes are reviewed using MySQL )Tj/F4 9.1 Tf (sys)Tj/F1 9.1 Tf ( schema views)Tj T* 7 0 Td (and representative business-cycle evidence.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 279.96 cm .14902 .196078 .219608 rg BT 13 TL/F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 7 16.9 Tm <7f20>Tj/F2 9.1 Tf (Granular AI-assisted engineering:)Tj/F1 9.1 Tf ( ChatGPT and AI agents are mapped across discovery, conversion, DMS, validation,)Tj T* 7 0 Td (tuning, cutover, troubleshooting, documentation, and decommission readiness.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 247.96 cm .14902 .196078 .219608 rg BT 13 TL/F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 7 16.9 Tm <7f20>Tj/F2 9.1 Tf (Measured outcome:)Tj/F1 9.1 Tf ( the migration completed with negligible issues; after approximately two months of stable target)Tj T* 7 0 Td (operation, the legacy Oracle source was decommissioned.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 1 1 rg 1 1 1 RG 84.0096 23.04724 34.415987 9.892759 re B Q q .08 .23 .38 rg .08 .23 .38 RG BT/helv 7.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 84.0096 24.547242 Tm[(TP-010 V6)]TJ ET Q

