.12549 .14902 .176471 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 42.8 Tm /F1 9.2 Tf 13 TL -0.019224 Tw (At approximately 50 TB, validation must be rigorous without becoming an avoidable extension of the migration window. AWS) Tj T* 0 Tw (DMS validation can provide useful evidence, but full validation at very large scale can add elapsed time and workload. The) Tj T* (modernization therefore benefits from an independent, repeatable audit layer driven by external Python scripts that query) Tj T* (Oracle 19c and Aurora MySQL directly and compare targeted metrics.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 52.8 599.36 cm
q
.180392 .435294 .619608 RG
.7 w
.917647 .94902 .972549 rg
n -8 -8 522.4 68 re B*
Q
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 42.7 Tm 13 TL /F2 9.3 Tf .090196 .227451 .368627 rg (Fast screening first; deep validation where evidence requires it. The audit framework can compare exact or) Tj T* (statistics-based row counts, table and partition sizes, LOB volumes, key/date ranges, NULL counts, business) Tj T* (aggregates, and selected checksums. During active CDC, comparisons must be taken at a consistent logical) Tj T* (checkpoint so normal transaction activity is not mistaken for migration loss.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 52.8 576.36 cm
q
.180392 .435294 .619608 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 2.5 Tm /F2 11.5 Tf 14 TL (16.1 Oracle 19c quick-validation queries) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 52.8 513.96 cm
%PreformattedPara
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 50.8 Tm /F3 6.6 Tf 8.2 TL (-- Exact row count \(use selectively on very large tables\)) Tj T* (SELECT COUNT\(*\) AS row_count FROM owner.table_name;) Tj T*  T* (-- Fast statistics-based row estimate) Tj T* (SELECT owner, table_name, num_rows, last_analyzed) Tj T* (FROM dba_tables) Tj T* (WHERE owner='OWNER' AND table_name='TABLE_NAME';) Tj T* ET
Q
q
1 0 0 1 52.8 416.76 cm
%PreformattedPara
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 83.6 Tm /F3 6.6 Tf 8.2 TL (-- Segment size) Tj T* (SELECT owner, segment_name,) Tj T* (       ROUND\(SUM\(bytes\)/POWER\(1024,3\),2\) AS size_gb) Tj T* (FROM dba_segments) Tj T* (WHERE owner='OWNER' AND segment_name='TABLE_NAME') Tj T* (GROUP BY owner, segment_name;) Tj T*  T* (-- CLOB volume) Tj T* (SELECT COUNT\(*\) AS row_count,) Tj T* (       ROUND\(SUM\(DBMS_LOB.GETLENGTH\(clob_column\)\)/POWER\(1024,3\),2\) AS clob_gb) Tj T* (FROM owner.table_name;) Tj T* ET
Q
q
1 0 0 1 52.8 395.76 cm
q
.180392 .435294 .619608 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 2.5 Tm /F2 11.5 Tf 14 TL (16.2 Aurora MySQL quick-validation queries) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 52.8 308.76 cm
%PreformattedPara
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 75.4 Tm /F3 6.6 Tf 8.2 TL (-- Exact row count) Tj T* (SELECT COUNT\(*\) AS row_count FROM schema_name.table_name;) Tj T*  T* (-- Fast table estimate and physical size) Tj T* (SELECT table_schema, table_name, table_rows,) Tj T* (       ROUND\(data_length/POWER\(1024,3\),2\) AS data_gb,) Tj T* (       ROUND\(index_length/POWER\(1024,3\),2\) AS index_gb,) Tj T* (       ROUND\(\(data_length+index_length\)/POWER\(1024,3\),2\) AS total_gb) Tj T* (FROM information_schema.tables) Tj T* (WHERE table_schema='schema_name' AND table_name='table_name';) Tj T* ET
Q
q
1 0 0 1 52.8 268.96 cm
%PreformattedPara
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 26.2 Tm /F3 6.6 Tf 8.2 TL (-- LONGTEXT volume) Tj T* (SELECT COUNT\(*\) AS row_count,) Tj T* (       ROUND\(SUM\(OCTET_LENGTH\(longtext_column\)\)/POWER\(1024,3\),2\) AS longtext_gb) Tj T* (FROM schema_name.table_name;) Tj T* ET
Q
 

